WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.259
For every WandaVision fan theory that turned
out to be right, there were many more times

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:07.319
WandaVision's story zigged when people thought
it would zag.

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:11.470
Many of us confidently identified early on
that Agnes was actually Agatha Harkness, who

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:15.530
would go on to be the show's big bad by season's
end, but that proved to be the exception and

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.910
not the rule.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.789
When Evan Peters turned up claiming to be
Wanda's dead brother Pietro Maximoff, for

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:25.840
example, people immediately leapt to the conclusion
that this was proof of a full-on X-Men-MCU

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:26.840
crossover.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.060
After all, Aaron Taylor-Johnson played Pietro
in the MCU's Age of Ultron, whereas Peters

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.200
was a part of the former Fox X-Men lineup.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.110
With the next Doctor Strange movie entitled
Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:40.930
there was every reason to suspect more of
Fox's mutants were on the way.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:44.550
Another major question arose thanks to a cheeky
comment Paul Bettany made in an interview

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:49.040
with Esquire indicating the show had one more
major cameo coming before season's end.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.040
Bettany said,

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.920
"It's an actor I've longed to work with all
my life, and we have some amazing scenes together

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.660
and the chemistry between us is, I think,
extraordinary and it was just fireworks on

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.660
set."

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.660
Who could it be?

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.220
Sir Ian McKellen as Magneto?

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.310
Maybe Mark Hamill?

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.050
The guesses were all over the place.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:08.250
In the end, both of these big questions were
answered in ways that punked fans a little.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.140
Peters was playing a nobody actor named Ralph
Bohner controlled by Agatha,

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.140
“Bohner?”

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.770
“Heh, Boner…”

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:20.770
and the actor Bettany had great chemistry
with was… himself as White Vision.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.700
Naturally, fans had pretty strong reactions
to the twin deceptions, and now Elizabeth

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.120
Olsen herself has stepped in to respond.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.830
In an interview with Variety, Olsen spoke
about fan theories, picking on both the true

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.439
identity of Pietro Maximoff and Bettany's
promise of a final "cameo."

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:35.439
She said,

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:39.249
"I knew that there are theories that had to
do with people wanting more surprises in cameos,

00:01:39.249 --> 00:01:42.409
but I'm not really that aware of what these
fan theories were, so I'm kind of learning

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:43.659
about it as we go.

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:46.950
Paul said something about this crazy cameo
when he was really just talking about doing

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:50.390
a scene with himself, and I know Paul thought
that was a really funny joke, and I thought

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:51.390
it was funny.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:55.520
But I was like, I think people are actually
going to suspect that there is more to come."

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:04.710
“I’m starting to believe that everything is meaningless.”

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:08.080
Spoiler: fans most certainly did think there
was more to come.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.689
As for Evan Peters playing Pietro, Olsen pointed
out that the possibility of a Fox-Disney crossover

00:02:12.689 --> 00:02:14.629
wasn't even on her radar yet.

00:02:14.629 --> 00:02:15.629
She said,

00:02:15.629 --> 00:02:17.680
"I didn't know about the multiverse when we
were filming this.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.280
So I wouldn't assume that that's what was
happening.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.610
I thought it was just a clever way to have
a Pietro.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.680
I didn't understand the larger plan of the
multiverse until I started working on 'Multiverse,'

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.939
or whatever our movie's called — the Doctor
Strange sequel!"

00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:32.150
It's worth noting that this is the second
occasion where a multiverse has been hinted

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.270
at but not delivered.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:35.560
“There are multiple realities Peter.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.129
This is Earth dimension 616 and I’m from
Earth 833.”

00:02:38.129 --> 00:02:41.740
“I’m sorry you’re saying there’s a
multiverse?”

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.450
The first time took place in Spider-Man: Far
From Home when Mysterio tricked people into

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:49.540
thinking he was from an alternate universe,
when he's actually just a very elaborate illusionist

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.540
and thief.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.950
Paul Bettany also weighed in on the topic
during an appearance on Good Morning America.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:55.370
He asked of the hosts,

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.709
"You know when you think something's gonna
be funny and then you say it and you actually

00:02:58.709 --> 00:02:59.750
panic about it?

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:03.739
Which is what I did because fans started guessing
who it might be, and they were guessing, like,

00:03:03.739 --> 00:03:05.709
Benedict Cumberbatch or Patrick Stewart.

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:09.049
I was thinking 'God that's a good idea,' and
they're gonna be so disappointed when they

00:03:09.049 --> 00:03:10.049
find out it's me."

00:03:10.049 --> 00:03:14.400
“Is it really you?”

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.550
While some fans may be annoyed at the subterfuge,
White Vision is an important part of the ongoing

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.090
Wanda and Vision love story.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:25.040
After all, with Westview's version of Vision
gone, the only hope Wanda currently has for

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.510
another chance with her husband is through
the White Vision - who was last seen flying

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.120
away to parts unknown.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.310
As for the Pietro fake-out, this isn't the
first time Marvel pulled something like this.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:38.560
In Iron Man 3, Sir Ben Kingsley was supposedly
cast to play The Mandarin, but turned out,

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.019
just like with Peters, to be an actor named
Trevor Slattery.

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:45.700
Of course, Evan Peters could still play Pietro
in the MCU someday — and Sir Patrick Stewart

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.010
or Sir Ian McKellen could turn up as mutants
eventually, too!

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:52.500
This could all be just a long con and the
multiverse is still upon us.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.500
Somehow.

